This chunk is from the Gemcitabine medical necessity drug coverage policy (G.E.H.A Medical Plans, administered via OncoHealth; reviewed 02/16/2026), in the "Universal Approval Criteria" section. It covers the list of accepted peer-reviewed journals for off-label use, exclusion of meeting abstracts and case reports, non-standard protocols, dose/frequency consistency requirements, and off-label review when a previously tried drug was discontinued for lack of efficacy. It applies to gemcitabine products (Gemzar J9201, Gemcitabine Accord J9196, Avgemsi J9184).

